gent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018LjkgoHwN4C1VcpVcCNmXS", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 133060, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0132p2GJY8S9tqb78dpMamC1", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. The staging build v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy. We rolled back all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. A human approver signed off on the rollback. After the rollback, the service is healthy in all regions on v2.3.0, with an error rate of 0.2%. Next step: find out what went wrong in v2.3.1 before deploying it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 133660, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0132p2GJY8S9tqb78dpMamC1", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 133660, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0132p2GJY8S9tqb78dpMamC1", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 137478, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy again, and SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open.\n\n- **The problem:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. Its staging build (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. A human approver signed off (\"Approved. Looks right.\") before it ran.\n- **Result:** All regions now report v2.3.0 and healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure and the rollback. Opening it paged the on-call engineer. The incident notes that someone needs to find out what went wrong in v2.3.1 before it's deployed again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019eRALEUVnJzGTLfAgAzsYU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0135R6XeTPjHbH3qqYAy3kbb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01YM9WaperpmkTeBGDgrdKer", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01N5JyZorxvriWjmVaHehUdx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018LjkgoHwN4C1VcpVcCNmXS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0132p2GJY8S9tqb78dpMamC1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. The staging build v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy. We rolled back all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. A human approver signed off on the rollback. After the rollback, the service is healthy in all regions on v2.3.0, with an error rate of 0.2%. Next step: find out what went wrong in v2.3.1 before deploying it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy again, and SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open.\n\n- **The problem:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. Its staging build (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. A human approver signed off (\"Approved. Looks right.\") before it ran.\n- **Result:** All regions now report v2.3.0 and healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure and the rollback. Opening it paged the on-call engineer. The incident notes that someone needs to find out what went wrong in v2.3.1 before it's deployed again.", "type": "text"}]}]}